  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: 
    basic: GLP1-R's seven helices are all alpha helices.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: 
    basic: Alpha helices are always right handed; Each turn is approximately 3.6
      amino acids in length.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: 
    basic: Membrane-spanning alpha helices are the most common structural motif in
      membrane proteins like GLP1-R.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: 
    basic: When GLP1 is bound to GLP1-R, there is an observable kink in the structure
      of one of GLP1-R's helices.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
